       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter amlodipine 50 mg once daily. Confirming the order doesn't change the limit. The labeled maximum is 10 mg per day, and 50 mg is five times that. I can't verify the patient details or any approvals, so I can't go above the labeled maximum on that basis.\n\nI can enter either of these right away:\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg by mouth once daily.** This is the usual starting dose.\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg by mouth once daily.** This is the maximum dose, if you want the full dose now.\n\nIf the blood pressure is severe enough that you think the patient needs more than this, I'd consider adding a second agent, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-type diuretic. For anything outside standard labeling, please talk with pharmacy or the attending. They can place the order through their own review process.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
